.TH RIO-OPEN 1
.SH NAME
rio-open \- open a path in rio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rio-open
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rio-open
opens a directory in vdir or a text file in rio's built-in editor.
It is used as a plumber start action in the Halatha guest.
Relative paths are resolved against the working directory.
If /dev/wctl is absent, it attaches to the rio service named by $wsys.
Binary files and files larger than four megabytes need another viewer.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/rio-open.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR rio (1),
.IR rio (4),
.IR vdir (1),
.IR plumber (4)
